# Financial data — never versioned
data/
data/**
*.qif
*.qfx
*.ofx
*.qfx
*.csv
!app/**/*.csv

# Local artifacts. *.db covers ledger.db; the replayed calls live beside it
# in ledger-replay.db (app/split_replay.py) and a compaction writes
# ledger-vacuumed.db for a moment — named here so nobody wonders.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
ledger-replay.db
ledger-vacuumed.db
# Backups go to ~/Backups/investment-app (backup.sh), never into the tree;
# a copy made here by hand is still a database and still ignored.
backups/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.DS_Store

# Research material — transcripts are third-party content, kept locally only
research/transcripts/
research/substack/
# research/x/ holds other people's posts. Its CONTENTS are excluded rather
# than the directory itself: git does not descend into an excluded directory,
# so "research/x/" followed by a negation silently keeps ignoring everything.
research/x/*
# The pull's setup steps and account list are configuration, not third-party
# content, and are useless to a reader if they are not in the repo.
!research/x/SETUP.md
!research/x/accounts.txt
research/*.log
# The working record of THIS ledger — round trips, net worth, income — and the
# scripts and notes that seed the owner's own calls. share.sh refuses them too;
# ignoring them here keeps a future `git add research` from tracking more.
research/audits/
research/seed-*
research/video/*.md
research/video/*.json
research/video/shots/
research/*.pdf

# Dev-only: playwright for the browser smoke test.
node_modules/

# Card and budget exports: real financial data, same as data/ generally.
data/cards/*.csv
data/budget/*.csv
logs
logs/

# Personal configuration: account overrides, tax profile, employer names.
config.json

# Personal source documents: kept locally, never shared.
*.pages

# Agent worktrees — transient, and each is its own git repo.
.claude/

# Video-transcription toolchain: a vendored build and a model, both large and
# both reproducible from research/video/setup.sh
research/video/vendor/
research/video/videoocr
